values ('2026-11-18', $terms$Effective date: November 18, 2026
Service provider: Metanomic, a Pennsylvania limited liability company
Contact: https://metanomic.ai/contact

These Terms of Service govern your use of Assistant Studio, including its dashboard, hosted chat assistants, embed script, and related features (the Service). “Metanomic,” “we,” and “us” refer to the company identified above. “You” refers to the person or organization that accepts these Terms.

1. Agreement and account eligibility

By selecting the checkbox agreeing to these Terms and creating an account, you agree to them. If you accept on behalf of an organization, you represent that you have authority to bind that organization, and the organization is the customer under these Terms.

You must be at least 18 years old and legally able to enter into this agreement. Provide accurate account information, keep your credentials secure, and notify us promptly if you suspect unauthorized access. You are responsible for the people you authorize to use your account and for their use of the Service.

2. What Assistant Studio provides

Assistant Studio lets you configure an AI assistant, supply knowledge documents, test the assistant, and publish it on approved websites using an embed script. Metanomic hosts the Service. You control where you install it, what knowledge you publish, and whether your assistant is live.

The free Starter plan is available subject to the limits shown in Studio or on the pricing page. Features marked “coming soon” are planned features. Joining a waitlist does not create a subscription, obligate you to pay, or guarantee access, pricing, or a release date. If Metanomic offers a paid plan, we will present its price, billing terms, and cancellation terms before you purchase it.

3. Your OpenAI key and charges

To generate answers, you must connect an OpenAI API key that you own or are authorized to use. You authorize Metanomic to store the key in encrypted form and use it to validate the connection and make OpenAI API requests on your behalf. Your use of OpenAI is subject to the terms and policies that apply to your OpenAI account.

OpenAI bills you directly for model usage, including your tests in Preview and requests from visitors to your published assistant. Metanomic does not add a markup to OpenAI token charges. You are responsible for monitoring usage, maintaining billing and model access, and configuring any available limits or alerts in your OpenAI account. Studio’s message limits and alerts help manage usage, but do not cap your OpenAI charges.

Your assistant may stop answering if your key is invalid or revoked, your account runs out of credit, a usage limit is reached, or the model provider is unavailable. You can unpublish your assistant and remove your key in Studio. You can also revoke the key directly with OpenAI.

4. Your content and generated answers

Your content remains yours. You retain your rights in the documents, instructions, and other materials you submit. You give Metanomic permission to host, copy, process, and transmit that material as needed to provide, secure, and support the Service. This includes sending relevant knowledge passages and instructions to OpenAI to generate answers. Metanomic does not use your content to train models.

You represent that you have the necessary rights and permissions to submit your content and use it in a public assistant. Published knowledge may be quoted or summarized to visitors. Publish only material you are willing to have disclosed to those visitors. If you supply a public source URL, you authorize us to display it with the answer. Keep those links accurate and current.

As between you and Metanomic, Metanomic claims no ownership of the answers generated for your assistant. Your ability to use those answers remains subject to applicable law, third-party rights, and the terms of your model provider. Generated answers may be similar to answers produced for others.

5. Your website and visitors

You must have permission to install the assistant on each approved website. You are responsible for its placement, configuration, instructions, knowledge, source links, and suitability for the people who use it. Keep your website’s privacy notice accurate, identify the assistant as AI, provide any notices or choices required for your use, and give visitors another way to reach you when they need help.

You must not ask visitors to enter passwords, API keys, payment card information, government identification numbers, health records, or other sensitive or confidential information. Do not use Assistant Studio to target children under 13 or knowingly collect their personal information through the assistant.

These Terms govern your relationship with Metanomic. Your website remains responsible for its own relationship with its visitors.

6. AI limitations and human oversight

AI-generated answers may be inaccurate, incomplete, misleading, or out of date. A citation identifies a document cited by the assistant. It does not certify that the document supports every statement in the answer. Some answers will have no citation.

Test your assistant before publishing it and after substantial changes to its instructions, knowledge, or model. Do not rely on it for emergencies, professional advice, or consequential decisions about people, including decisions involving employment, credit, housing, healthcare, or access to essential services. Provide human review when an error could materially affect a visitor. Studio assistants answer questions and can display source links. They cannot complete transactions or take external actions for visitors.

7. Acceptable use

You may not use the Service to:

• Break the law, infringe intellectual property or privacy rights, distribute malware, commit fraud, or impersonate someone deceptively.
• Publish material you do not have permission to disclose or use the assistant to collect protected information.
• Circumvent authentication, website restrictions, or usage limits, access another customer’s information, or intentionally interfere with the Service.
• Violate the model provider’s applicable usage policies or use the Service for unauthorized bulk requests or abusive traffic.

Metanomic may remove unlawful material or restrict access when reasonably necessary to address a violation, security issue, suspected compromise, or threat to the Service or another person.

8. Privacy and data handling

The Assistant Studio Data and Privacy notice (https://metanomic.ai/assistant-studio/privacy) explains what Metanomic stores and how the embedded chat handles data. Metanomic stores account information, settings, knowledge documents, encrypted keys, and usage records. Studio does not store conversation transcripts in its database. Recent messages, assistant instructions, and relevant knowledge passages are sent to OpenAI to generate answers. Metanomic requests responses with storage disabled. Hosting and model providers may retain operational or abuse-monitoring records under their own policies.

If your deployment needs specific retention, data residency, or contractual data-processing terms, contact Metanomic before publishing. Any such commitments must be set out in a separate written agreement.

9. Availability, changes, and support

We may update features, supported models, or plan limits as the Service evolves. We aim to give reasonable advance notice of material reductions where practicable. Security, legal, and provider changes may require faster action.

The free plan does not include a guaranteed uptime, response time, or support commitment. Contact us through the Metanomic contact form (https://metanomic.ai/contact) for help. Keep your own copies of your knowledge documents and any settings you need to retain.

10. Suspension, termination, and deletion

You may stop using the Service at any time. You can unpublish your assistant from Studio and remove the embed script from your website. To fully remove the integration from your site, remove the script. If you are eligible for self-service account deletion, you may delete your account in Studio. Shared Metanomic administrator accounts are handled separately.

We may suspend or terminate access for a material violation, a material risk to users or the Service, a legal requirement, or discontinuation of the Service. Where reasonable, we will give notice and a chance to correct a remediable violation. We may act immediately when delay would increase risk or conflict with a legal obligation.

Deletion removes the associated Studio records from the active database as described in the privacy notice. Backup copies, operational records, and information providers retain under their own policies may remain for a limited period. Provisions that by their nature apply after termination, including ownership, liability, disputes, and accrued obligations, survive termination.

11. Warranties and liability

To the extent permitted by applicable law, the Service is provided “as is” and “as available.” Metanomic disclaims implied warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and noninfringement. We do not warrant uninterrupted operation, compatibility with every website, or the accuracy or completeness of AI-generated answers.

To the extent permitted by applicable law, neither party is liable to the other for indirect, incidental, special, or consequential damages, or for lost profits, arising from the Service or these Terms. Metanomic’s total liability for all claims arising from the Service or these Terms will not exceed the greater of US$100 or the amount you paid Metanomic for Assistant Studio in the 12 months before the event giving rise to the claim. Payments to OpenAI are separate from fees paid to Metanomic.

This section does not limit liability for fraud, willful misconduct, or gross negligence, or any liability or remedy that applicable law does not allow the parties to limit. Nothing in these Terms waives mandatory consumer protections.

12. Third-party claims arising from business use

If you use the Service on behalf of a business, you agree to indemnify Metanomic for reasonable costs and damages arising from a third-party claim to the extent caused by your unlawful use, your infringement of third-party rights through content you supplied, or your material breach of Sections 5 or 7. This obligation does not apply to the extent Metanomic caused the claim. Metanomic will give you prompt notice and reasonable cooperation. Neither party may settle a claim in a way that admits fault or imposes obligations on the other without that party’s consent.

13. Governing law and disputes

Pennsylvania law governs these Terms, without regard to its conflict-of-laws rules, subject to mandatory rights that apply where you live or do business. Before filing suit, each party should make a good-faith effort to resolve the dispute by contacting the other. This does not prevent either party from seeking urgent relief or filing in time to preserve a claim.

For business customers, court proceedings must be brought in a Pennsylvania state court or a federal court in Pennsylvania with jurisdiction. Consumers retain any forum and small-claims rights available under applicable law.

14. Changes to these Terms and notices

We will post updates with a new effective date. For material changes, we will provide reasonable advance notice by email or in Studio where practicable, and request renewed acceptance when required. If you do not agree to a change, you may stop using the Service before it takes effect and close your account. Updates will not retroactively change the terms governing an existing dispute without agreement.

We may send service and account notices to the email address associated with your account or through Studio. Send legal notices through the Metanomic contact form listed at the top of these Terms. If any provision is unenforceable, the remaining provisions continue to apply. These Terms and any separately accepted written agreement for Assistant Studio constitute the agreement for the Service. A separately signed agreement controls where it expressly conflicts with these Terms.$terms$);
